<Concept title="Trap counterplay and recovery" section="States">
  <p>This contract covers issues #94, #738, #724, #737, #592, #341,
  #345, #473 and the repeat-completion portion of #62. It defines the remake
  behavior exercised by this batch; it does not claim complete original parity.</p>
  <h2>Inventory and recovery</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each character MUST save inventory order as an explicit ordered list of
    item IDs alongside quantities. JSON key sorting MUST NOT change manual order.
    Unknown/duplicate order entries MUST be ignored; unlisted items MUST be retained.
    Legacy saves without a list MUST retain their available dictionary order.</li>
    <li>On a lethal field hit, one held Scape Doll MUST be consumed before defeat
    is emitted. HP MUST become full; harmful statuses MUST clear; the current
    encounter and meseta MUST remain unchanged. Recovery grants two seconds of
    damage/status immunity (remake tuning), with the existing stand-up animation.
    Without a doll the existing defeat transaction MUST run exactly once.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Trap counterplay</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Dormant field balls MUST be visible and attackable to CASTs and to characters
    with Trap Vision. Arming MUST reveal the ball to everybody. Hidden balls MUST
    NOT steal targeting or projectile hits. Revealed hostile balls MUST disarm on
    a damaging weapon contact, without detonating or awarding enemy EXP/drops.</li>
    <li>Player traps MUST NOT be treated as enemies. Only one player trap may be live:
    replacing it MUST expire the previous one without a blast. Placement MUST be
    refused without consumption outside a field, by non-CASTs, or while defeated.</li>
    <li>Trap Vision retains the existing 60-second wall-clock duration and refreshes
    to the later expiry; it MUST survive room changes but MUST reset when changing
    characters, ending/resetting a session, or dying. City/dead use MUST NOT consume it.
    These duration/scope choices are remake rules, not recovered PSZ measurements.</li>
    <li>A hostile trap contact MUST resolve damage and status under the same dodge,
    recovery and defeat guards. Healing MUST NOT revive a defeated player.
    A spent/disarmed trap MUST NOT trigger or apply its payload twice.</li>
    <li>Trigger range and blast range MUST be represented separately. This batch
    does not claim that the existing 4-unit hostile radius or 60 Hz fuse divisor
    matches the original. Exact timing/radii and Light Trap confusion remain #607/#724
    research work; the existing stun substitute MUST remain labelled as such.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Status delivery and support</h2>
  <p>The 3D player MUST accept the currently supported trap payloads: freeze,
  burn and the temporary stun substitute. Existing project duration/potency values
  are used, not newly asserted original-game numbers. Duplicate effects MUST NOT
  stack or refresh. Burn ticks MUST use elapsed gameplay time and stop on cure,
  death or expiry. Once inflicted, burn MUST NOT be dodged and MUST NOT interrupt
  movement or break freeze. Anti MUST clear player ailments; Resta MUST heal the living
  player, using the learned level and the existing support power table. CAST
  characters MUST NOT cast through stale palette entries. Neither support cast may emit the offensive fallback fire projectile.
  Reverser and the still-unimplemented 3D buffs/debuffs (Shifta, Deband, Jellen,
  Zalure) MUST reject the cast without spending PP and show feedback. They remain
  follow-up work in #345.</p>
  <p>Sol Atomizer MUST cure the living field player's active ailments and consume
  one item only when there is an ailment to cure. It MUST NOT restore HP. A Moon
  Atomizer without a supported downed teammate MUST be rejected without consumption;
  it MUST NOT act as a full self-heal. Companion revival remains follow-up work.</p>
  <h2>Rendering and boss completion</h2>
  <p>Bear and needle traps MUST use instance-owned materials with the storybook's
  per-surface UV transforms and repeat/mirror axes. Off states MUST hide only their
  active surfaces. Armed bear prongs MUST scroll; releasing a caught player MUST NOT
  overwrite damage, defeat or revival state. Room teardown MUST release a surviving
  hold. This is project visual parity, not a claim that storybook tuning
  reproduces the DS material. Trap-ball overrides MUST preserve source tint/alpha.</p>
  <p>Repeated room-clear checks MUST NOT create multiple boss return warps. Objective
  updates after the fight MUST still be able to unlock a deferred exit.</p>
  <p>Dialog boxes MUST own a copy of their page array; closing a dialog MUST NOT
  clear the caller's constant/read-only data. This regression was observed during
  the field-entry matrix and is covered by the seeded test.</p>
  <h2>Verification</h2>
  <p>Seeded test-runner cases cover save reconstruction, recovery guards and trap
  state boundaries. The gameplay batch probe exercises real actors/materials,
  hurtbox contacts and support delivery. Human playtesting covers visual quality,
  trap readability and full boss runs; passing logic checks does not close those gaps.</p>
</Concept>
